# Contributing

Open an issue before large changes. Never include passwords, session files,
tokens, workout exports, location data or unredacted logs. Use synthetic data.

Create a Python 3.12+ virtual environment, then run:
```text
python -m pip install -e ".[dev,remote]"
python -m pytest -q
```

Create a feature branch, make changes, submit a pull request, pass checks, then
merge. Do not push directly to the default branch. Describe behavior and tests.
Preserve fixed operation allowlists, explicit units, bounded responses, local
OAuth consent, PKCE, audience validation and separate write permissions. Do not
add arbitrary endpoints. Update documentation and CHANGELOG; synchronize
VERSION and pyproject.toml. Installation regenerates the local interpreter path
in the plugin manifest; do not commit a machine-specific path.

CI and default tests must remain offline. Live checks are opt-in:
`python scripts/verify_live.py`; they read an account but print only check results.
Verify unauthenticated remote calls return 401. Never disable TLS verification.
For vulnerabilities, use GitHub private reporting if available or contact the
maintainer privately before publishing details. Contributions use the MIT license.

Documentation-only maintenance can retain the existing VERSION when runtime/API
behavior is unchanged. Preserve dated historical audit results and distinguish
owner-reported behavior from independently verified protocol/account tests.

After merging a PR, remove its local branch only after verifying the branch head
matches the merged PR's final head (squash merges need this check because Git
ancestry alone may report the branch unmerged). Keep main tracking origin/main.
Discard only known disposable caches/build artifacts. Preserve encrypted live
write journals, audit records, credentials, active runtime environments and logs
needed for unresolved outcomes. Never publish private audit artifacts.

Quality gates: critical Python lint across source/scripts/tests, strict typed
launcher/diagnostic interfaces, package build, tracked secret/private-artifact
checks and dependency audit. Legacy modules do not yet have complete strict
type coverage. Desktop/frozen/container checks are separate offline CI jobs.

Documentation belongs under the categorized docs/ tree; see [documentation maintenance](docs/development/documentation.md). Run `python scripts/check_docs.py` after moving pages or changing links/contracts. Keep the README focused on user value and the starting path. Describe this project on its own without direct comparisons to other projects, retain dated audits, and never describe watch execution as verified from server readback.
